.TH BOOTSTRAP.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-dataformat-viewer t01.00.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
bootstrap.sh \- create the data format viewer's Python virtual environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./bootstrap.sh
.RB [ \-\-dev ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Checks that
.B $PYTHON
(default
.BR python3 )
is 3.9 or newer, creates
.I venv/
next to the script if absent, upgrades pip, installs
.B mu2edaq\-discovery
if it is not importable (editable from
.I ../mu2edaq\-discovery
when that directory exists, otherwise from GitHub, best effort), then
installs
.I requirements.txt
(PyYAML, PyQt6).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-dev
Also install pytest.
The package has no tests.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the script's header comment.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PYTHON
Interpreter used to create the venv.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 if Python is missing or too old; 2 on an unknown option;
otherwise the failing command's status
.RB ( "set \-euo pipefail" ).
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
\&./bootstrap.sh
PYTHON=/usr/bin/python3.9 ./bootstrap.sh
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR start\-mu2edaq\-dataformat\-viewer.sh (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ group, Fermilab.
